IMPORT prelude

-- Minnesota Statutes, chapter 290 (income and franchise taxes): what a full-year Minnesota resident individual owes and
-- gets back. Resident (290.01, subd. 7); net income from federal adjusted gross income (290.01, subds. 19, 22; additions
-- 290.0131 and subtractions 290.0132 as totals, except three worked out: the Social Security subtraction (290.0132, subd.
-- 26), the standard or itemized deduction (subd. 19 with 290.0123 and 290.0122, subd. 2) and the dependent exemption (subd.
-- 20 with 290.0121)); the rate schedules (290.06, subd. 2c) with the bracket adjustment of subd. 2d; the Minnesota child tax
-- credit (290.0661) and working family credit (290.0671), phased out jointly and refundable.
--
-- SEAT: the individual Minnesota resident (or the married couple filing jointly): "How much Minnesota income tax do I owe,
-- and how much child tax credit and working family credit do I get?" The commissioner's duty to refund the excess of the
-- refundable credits is written as a regulative rule.
--
-- Edition: Minnesota Statutes 2025 (Office of the Revisor of Statutes, retrieved 2026-10-19), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mn-stat-ch-290-2025.txt. The 2026 Regular Session's amendments (listed in the file's header,
-- among them 290.06, subd. 2c) are NOT in the deposited text and are not encoded.
--
-- INFLATION ADJUSTMENT. Every dollar amount used here is "adjusted for inflation ... as provided in section 270C.22" from a
-- stated statutory year (2019, 2023 or 2025). Section 270C.22 is not deposited, so the adjustment for each statutory year is
-- an input factor (1 for the statutory year itself); the encoding applies each provision's own rounding rule to the product.
--
-- Federal terms (federal AGI, IRC s 32 eligibility and qualifying child, s 86 provisional income and taxable Social Security,
-- s 151/152 dependants, s 2 filing status) are inputs; the federal encoding is subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986/.
--
-- NOT ENCODED (answers `not covered` where a question can reach it): nonresidents and part-year residents (290.06, subd.
-- 2c(e); 290.0661, subd. 5); an individual who is a dependant of another taxpayer (290.0123, subd. 3); a married individual
-- filing separately whose spouse itemizes (290.0123, subd. 4(1)); the tax tables of 290.06, subd. 2c(d); advance payments
-- and the minimum credit (290.0661, subds. 8, 9); the allocation for earned income not subject to tax (290.0671, subd. 1(e));
-- all other credits; the alternative minimum tax (290.091); filing and payment (ch. 289A, not deposited).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Minnesota individual income tax -- Minnesota Statutes chapter 290`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `a nonresident or part-year resident is not encoded (290.06, subd. 2c(e))`
    `an individual who is a dependent of another taxpayer is not encoded (290.0123, subd. 3)`
    `a married individual filing separately whose spouse itemizes has no standard deduction (290.0123, subd. 4(1)); itemized deductions for that case are not encoded`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Filing status and rounding`

DECLARE `Filing status` IS ONE OF
    `single`
    `married filing separately`
    `married filing jointly`
    `head of household`
    `surviving spouse`

GIVEN `text` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Filing status`
`the filing status named` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `text` EQUALS "married filing jointly"    THEN `married filing jointly`
        IF `text` EQUALS "married filing separately" THEN `married filing separately`
        IF `text` EQUALS "head of household"         THEN `head of household`
        IF `text` EQUALS "surviving spouse"          THEN `surviving spouse`
        OTHERWISE `single`

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `joint or surviving spouse` IF
    `status` EQUALS `married filing jointly` OR `status` EQUALS `surviving spouse`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `x` AT LEAST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS IF `x` AT MOST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

-- 290.06, subd. 2d and 290.0132, subd. 26(j): "rounded to the nearest $10 amount. If the rate bracket ends in $5, it must
-- be rounded up".
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest $10` MEANS FLOOR ((`x` PLUS 5) DIVIDED BY 10) TIMES 10

-- 290.0121, subd. 3 and 290.0123, subd. 6: "rounded down to the nearest $50 amount".
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded down to the nearest $50` MEANS FLOOR (`x` DIVIDED BY 50) TIMES 50

-- 290.0661, subd. 7(a): "rounded to the nearest $60" (a value halfway is taken up: NOTES.md).
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest $60` MEANS FLOOR ((`x` PLUS 30) DIVIDED BY 60) TIMES 60

-- An amount for a year after its statutory year: the amount times the factor, rounded as the provision says. For the
-- statutory year itself (factor 1) the provisions make no adjustment, so the amount stands unrounded (290.0122, subd. 2(e),
-- 290.0123, subd. 6 and 290.0661, subd. 7 adjust only "for taxable years beginning after" the statutory year).
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER, `factor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`adjusted, rounded down to $50` MEANS
    IF `factor` EQUALS 1 THEN `amount` ELSE `rounded down to the nearest $50` (`amount` TIMES `factor`)

GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER, `factor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`adjusted, rounded to $10` MEANS
    IF `factor` EQUALS 1 THEN `amount` ELSE `rounded to the nearest $10` (`amount` TIMES `factor`)

GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER, `factor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`adjusted, rounded to $60` MEANS
    IF `factor` EQUALS 1 THEN `amount` ELSE `rounded to the nearest $60` (`amount` TIMES `factor`)

-- The three adjustment factors, one per statutory year (270C.22, not deposited, gives them).
DECLARE `Inflation factors` HAS
    `since 2019` IS A NUMBER
    `since 2023` IS A NUMBER
    `since 2025` IS A NUMBER

§§ `290.01, subd. 7 -- am I a resident`

-- (a): "any individual domiciled in Minnesota" (the 911(d) exception for qualified individuals abroad is out); (b): also an
-- individual "domiciled outside the state who maintains a place of abode in the state and spends in the aggregate more than
-- one-half of the tax year in Minnesota, unless: (1) the individual or the spouse ... is in the armed forces ...; or (2) the
-- individual is covered under the reciprocity provisions in section 290.081". "Presence within the state for any part of a
-- calendar day constitutes a day spent in the state."
@export Am I a Minnesota resident for income tax (Minn. Stat. 290.01, subd. 7)?
GIVEN `domiciled in Minnesota` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Minnesota is your domicile (your permanent home)
      `abode in Minnesota` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you keep a place to live in Minnesota (owned or rented by you or your spouse, occupied or not)
      `days in Minnesota` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of the tax year you were in Minnesota for any part of the day
      `days in the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days the tax year has (365, or 366 in a leap year)
      `armed forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse is in the United States armed forces
      `reciprocity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are covered by Minnesota's income tax reciprocity with your home state (section 290.081)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a Minnesota resident` IF
        `domiciled in Minnesota`
    OR  (    `abode in Minnesota`
         AND `days in Minnesota` GREATER THAN (`days in the tax year` DIVIDED BY 2)
         AND (NOT `armed forces`)
         AND (NOT `reciprocity`))

§§ `290.0132, subd. 26 -- the Social Security subtraction`

-- (a): "the greater of the simplified subtraction ... or the alternate subtraction". (b)-(d): the taxable Social Security
-- benefits, reduced by 10% for each $4,000 (married filing separately: $2,000), "or fraction thereof", of AGI over the
-- phaseout threshold: $100,000 joint or surviving spouse; $78,000 single or head of household; half the joint figure for a
-- separate return. (e)-(h): the lesser of taxable benefits and a maximum: $5,840 joint, less 20% of provisional income over
-- $88,630; $4,560 single or head of household, less 20% over $69,250; for a separate return half the joint maximum, less 20%
-- over "one-half the threshold amount specified in paragraph (d)" (paragraph (d) specifies none: read as (f), NOTES.md
-- finding 2). (j): only the (c)(1), (2) thresholds are adjusted (statutory year 2023, nearest $10).
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
      `taxable Social Security benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
      `provisional income` IS A NUMBER
      `factors` IS AN `Inflation factors`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Social Security subtraction` MEANS
    `the larger of` `simplified` `alternate`
    WHERE
        `joint threshold` MEANS `adjusted, rounded to $10` 100000 (`factors`'s `since 2023`)
        `threshold` MEANS
            CONSIDER `status`
            WHEN `married filing jointly` THEN `joint threshold`
            WHEN `surviving spouse` THEN `joint threshold`
            WHEN `married filing separately` THEN `joint threshold` DIVIDED BY 2
            OTHERWISE `adjusted, rounded to $10` 78000 (`factors`'s `since 2023`)
        `step` MEANS IF `status` EQUALS `married filing separately` THEN 2000 ELSE 4000
        `steps over` MEANS CEILING ((`the larger of` 0 (`adjusted gross income` MINUS `threshold`)) DIVIDED BY `step`)
        `simplified` MEANS `the larger of` 0 (`taxable Social Security benefits` TIMES (1 MINUS (10% TIMES `steps over`)))
        `maximum` MEANS
            CONSIDER `status`
            WHEN `married filing jointly` THEN `the larger of` 0 (5840 MINUS (20% TIMES (`the larger of` 0 (`provisional income` MINUS 88630))))
            WHEN `surviving spouse` THEN `the larger of` 0 (5840 MINUS (20% TIMES (`the larger of` 0 (`provisional income` MINUS 88630))))
            WHEN `married filing separately` THEN `the larger of` 0 (2920 MINUS (20% TIMES (`the larger of` 0 (`provisional income` MINUS 44315))))
            OTHERWISE `the larger of` 0 (4560 MINUS (20% TIMES (`the larger of` 0 (`provisional income` MINUS 69250))))
        `alternate` MEANS `the smaller of` `taxable Social Security benefits` `maximum`

§§ `290.0123, 290.0122 -- the standard deduction or itemized deductions`

-- 290.0123, subd. 1: $27,650 for a joint filer or surviving spouse; $20,800 head of household; "for any other filer,
-- one-half the amount in clause (1)"; plus subd. 2: $1,450 for a taxpayer 65 or over ($1,850 if not married or a surviving
-- spouse), the same for blindness, and $1,450 each for a spouse 65 or over or blind. Subd. 6: adjusted from 2023, rounded down
-- to $50; the separate amount is half the adjusted joint amount.
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
      `taxpayer 65 or over` IS A BOOLEAN
      `taxpayer blind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse 65 or over` IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse blind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `factors` IS AN `Inflation factors`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the standard deduction before the limit` MEANS
    `basic` PLUS `additional`
    WHERE
        `f` MEANS `factors`'s `since 2023`
        `joint` MEANS `adjusted, rounded down to $50` 27650 `f`
        `basic` MEANS
            CONSIDER `status`
            WHEN `married filing jointly` THEN `joint`
            WHEN `surviving spouse` THEN `joint`
            WHEN `head of household` THEN `adjusted, rounded down to $50` 20800 `f`
            OTHERWISE `joint` DIVIDED BY 2
        `married` MEANS `status` EQUALS `married filing jointly` OR `status` EQUALS `married filing separately` OR `status` EQUALS `surviving spouse`
        `own amount` MEANS
            IF `married` THEN `adjusted, rounded down to $50` 1450 `f` ELSE `adjusted, rounded down to $50` 1850 `f`
        `spouse amount` MEANS `adjusted, rounded down to $50` 1450 `f`
        `additional` MEANS
            sum (LIST
                (IF `taxpayer 65 or over` THEN `own amount` ELSE 0),
                (IF `taxpayer blind` THEN `own amount` ELSE 0),
                (IF `spouse 65 or over` THEN `spouse amount` ELSE 0),
                (IF `spouse blind` THEN `spouse amount` ELSE 0))

-- 290.0123, subd. 5 (and 290.0122, subd. 2 for itemized deductions, in the same words): with AGI over $220,650, reduced by
-- the lesser of 3% of the excess over $220,650 up to $304,970 plus 10% of AGI over $304,970, or 80% of the deduction; over
-- $1,000,000, reduced by 80%; for a separate return, half the AGI amounts. Adjusted from 2023, rounded down to $50.
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
      `adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
      `deduction` IS A NUMBER
      `factors` IS AN `Inflation factors`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction after the high-income limit` MEANS
    `deduction` MINUS `the reduction`
    WHERE
        `f` MEANS `factors`'s `since 2023`
        `half` MEANS IF `status` EQUALS `married filing separately` THEN 0.5 ELSE 1
        `low` MEANS (`adjusted, rounded down to $50` 220650 `f`) TIMES `half`
        `high` MEANS (`adjusted, rounded down to $50` 304970 `f`) TIMES `half`
        `million` MEANS (`adjusted, rounded down to $50` 1000000 `f`) TIMES `half`
        `formula` MEANS
                (3% TIMES (`the larger of` 0 ((`the smaller of` `adjusted gross income` `high`) MINUS `low`)))
            PLUS (10% TIMES (`the larger of` 0 (`adjusted gross income` MINUS `high`)))
        `the reduction` MEANS
            IF `adjusted gross income` GREATER THAN `million`
            THEN 80% TIMES `deduction`
            ELSE `the smaller of` `formula` (80% TIMES `deduction`)

§§ `290.0121 -- the dependent exemption`

-- Subd. 1: $4,250 times the number of dependants (IRC ss 151, 152), less the disallowed amount. Subd. 2: the applicable
-- percentage is 2 points for each $2,500 (separate return: $1,250) "or fraction of that amount" of AGI over the threshold:
-- $291,950 joint or surviving spouse; $243,300 head of household; $194,650 single; half the joint figure for a separate
-- return; at most 100%. Subd. 3: adjusted from 2019, rounded down to $50.
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
      `number of dependents` IS A NUMBER
      `adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
      `factors` IS AN `Inflation factors`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dependent exemption` MEANS
    `the larger of` 0 (`full` MINUS (`full` TIMES `the applicable percentage`))
    WHERE
        `f` MEANS `factors`'s `since 2019`
        `full` MEANS (`adjusted, rounded down to $50` 4250 `f`) TIMES `number of dependents`
        `joint threshold` MEANS `adjusted, rounded down to $50` 291950 `f`
        `threshold` MEANS
            CONSIDER `status`
            WHEN `married filing jointly` THEN `joint threshold`
            WHEN `surviving spouse` THEN `joint threshold`
            WHEN `married filing separately` THEN `joint threshold` DIVIDED BY 2
            WHEN `head of household` THEN `adjusted, rounded down to $50` 243300 `f`
            OTHERWISE `adjusted, rounded down to $50` 194650 `f`
        `step` MEANS IF `status` EQUALS `married filing separately` THEN 1250 ELSE 2500
        `the applicable percentage` MEANS
            `the smaller of` 1 (2% TIMES CEILING ((`the larger of` 0 (`adjusted gross income` MINUS `threshold`)) DIVIDED BY `step`))

§§ `290.06, subds. 2c, 2d -- the tax`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `low` IS A NUMBER, `high` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part of` MEANS `the larger of` 0 ((`the smaller of` `x` `high`) MINUS `low`)

-- (a) joint and surviving spouse: 5.35% on the first $38,770; 6.8% to $154,020; 7.85% to $269,010; 9.85% above. Separate
-- returns: "one-half of the above amounts after the adjustment required in subdivision 2d". (b) unmarried: $26,520,
-- $87,110, $161,720. (c) head of household: $32,650, $131,190, $214,980. Subd. 2d: adjusted from 2019, nearest $10.
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
      `taxable net income` IS A NUMBER
      `factors` IS AN `Inflation factors`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax under 290.06, subd. 2c` MEANS
    sum (LIST
        (5.35% TIMES (`the part of` `taxable net income` 0 `b1`)),
        (6.8% TIMES (`the part of` `taxable net income` `b1` `b2`)),
        (7.85% TIMES (`the part of` `taxable net income` `b2` `b3`)),
        (9.85% TIMES (`the part of` `taxable net income` `b3` 1000000000000)))
    WHERE
        `f` MEANS `factors`'s `since 2019`
        `b1` MEANS
            CONSIDER `status`
            WHEN `married filing jointly` THEN `adjusted, rounded to $10` 38770 `f`
            WHEN `surviving spouse` THEN `adjusted, rounded to $10` 38770 `f`
            WHEN `married filing separately` THEN (`adjusted, rounded to $10` 38770 `f`) DIVIDED BY 2
            WHEN `head of household` THEN `adjusted, rounded to $10` 32650 `f`
            OTHERWISE `adjusted, rounded to $10` 26520 `f`
        `b2` MEANS
            CONSIDER `status`
            WHEN `married filing jointly` THEN `adjusted, rounded to $10` 154020 `f`
            WHEN `surviving spouse` THEN `adjusted, rounded to $10` 154020 `f`
            WHEN `married filing separately` THEN (`adjusted, rounded to $10` 154020 `f`) DIVIDED BY 2
            WHEN `head of household` THEN `adjusted, rounded to $10` 131190 `f`
            OTHERWISE `adjusted, rounded to $10` 87110 `f`
        `b3` MEANS
            CONSIDER `status`
            WHEN `married filing jointly` THEN `adjusted, rounded to $10` 269010 `f`
            WHEN `surviving spouse` THEN `adjusted, rounded to $10` 269010 `f`
            WHEN `married filing separately` THEN (`adjusted, rounded to $10` 269010 `f`) DIVIDED BY 2
            WHEN `head of household` THEN `adjusted, rounded to $10` 214980 `f`
            OTHERWISE `adjusted, rounded to $10` 161720 `f`

§§ `290.0661, 290.0671 -- the child tax credit and the working family credit`

-- 290.0671, subd. 1(a): to receive the working family credit a resident "must be eligible for a credit under section 32",
-- except that (1) a taxpayer with no qualifying children aged 19 to 64 "may also receive a credit", (2) the s 32 income limits
-- do not apply and (3) s 32(m) does not apply (asked as one fact). (b): "four percent of the first $8,750 of earned income";
-- (c): plus $925 for one "qualifying older child" (a s 32(c) qualifying child aged at least 18 in the year, subd. 1a), $2,100
-- for two, $2,500 for three or more. Subd. 7: adjusted from 2023 (no rounding rule is stated).
-- 290.0661, subd. 1: a "qualifying child" is a s 32(c) qualifying child under 18; subd. 2: a resident eligible for the
-- working family credit (or who would be but for too little earned income); subd. 3: "$1,750 per qualifying child"; subd. 7:
-- adjusted from 2025, nearest $60. Subd. 4: "The combined amount of the credits is reduced by 12 percent of earned income or
-- adjusted gross income, whichever is greater, in excess of the phaseout threshold": $35,000 joint, $29,500 all others
-- (adjusted from 2023, no rounding stated). 290.0671, subd. 1(d): for a taxpayer with qualifying older children "who did not
-- qualify for the credit under section 290.0661, the phaseout rate equals nine percent". Both refundable (290.0661, subd. 6;
-- 290.0671, subd. 4).
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
      `eligible under 290.0671, subd. 1(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `earned income` IS A NUMBER
      `adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
      `qualifying children under 18` IS A NUMBER
      `qualifying older children` IS A NUMBER
      `factors` IS AN `Inflation factors`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the combined credits after the phaseout` MEANS
    IF (NOT `eligible under 290.0671, subd. 1(a)`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the larger of` 0 ((`child tax credit` PLUS `working family credit`) MINUS `the phaseout`)
    WHERE
        `f23` MEANS `factors`'s `since 2023`
        `child tax credit` MEANS (`adjusted, rounded to $60` 1750 (`factors`'s `since 2025`)) TIMES `qualifying children under 18`
        `older amount` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `qualifying older children` AT LEAST 3 THEN 2500 TIMES `f23`
                IF `qualifying older children` EQUALS 2 THEN 2100 TIMES `f23`
                IF `qualifying older children` EQUALS 1 THEN 925 TIMES `f23`
                OTHERWISE 0
        `working family credit` MEANS (4% TIMES (`the smaller of` `earned income` (8750 TIMES `f23`))) PLUS `older amount`
        `threshold` MEANS IF `status` EQUALS `married filing jointly` THEN 35000 TIMES `f23` ELSE 29500 TIMES `f23`
        `rate` MEANS
            IF `qualifying older children` AT LEAST 1 AND `qualifying children under 18` EQUALS 0 THEN 9% ELSE 12%
        `the phaseout` MEANS `rate` TIMES (`the larger of` 0 ((`the larger of` `earned income` `adjusted gross income`) MINUS `threshold`))

@export How much Minnesota child tax credit and working family credit (combined, after the joint phaseout) do I get (290.0661, 290.0671)?
GIVEN `filing status` IS A STRING @desc Your federal filing status. One of: "single", "married filing separately", "married filing jointly", "head of household", "surviving spouse"
      `eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a Minnesota resident who would be eligible for the federal earned income credit (s 32), ignoring the federal income limits and s 32(m); a taxpayer with no qualifying children aged 19 to 64 also counts
      `earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your earned income for the year (wages and self-employment earnings, as for the federal earned income credit), in US dollars
      `federal AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `children under 18` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying children (federal earned income credit rules) you have who were under 18 all year
      `older children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying children you have who reached 18 or older during the year (for example full-time students under 24)
      `factor since 2019` IS A NUMBER @desc The inflation adjustment from 2019 under section 270C.22 for the year (1 for 2019); not used by this question
      `factor since 2023` IS A NUMBER @desc The inflation adjustment from 2023 under section 270C.22 for the year (1 for 2023)
      `factor since 2025` IS A NUMBER @desc The inflation adjustment from 2025 under section 270C.22 for the year (1 for 2025)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much child tax credit and working family credit do I get` MEANS
    `the combined credits after the phaseout` (`the filing status named` `filing status`) `eligible` `earned income` `federal AGI` `children under 18` `older children`
        (`Inflation factors` WITH `since 2019` IS `factor since 2019`, `since 2023` IS `factor since 2023`, `since 2025` IS `factor since 2025`)

§§ `The whole return`

DECLARE `My Minnesota tax` HAS
    `net income`                          IS A NUMBER
    `tax before credits`                  IS A NUMBER
    `child tax credit and working family credit` IS A NUMBER
    `tax after credits, or refund if negative` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `My Minnesota return` HAS
    `filing status`                       IS A `Filing status`
    `federal adjusted gross income`       IS A NUMBER
    `additions`                           IS A NUMBER
    `other subtractions`                  IS A NUMBER
    `taxable Social Security benefits`    IS A NUMBER
    `provisional income`                  IS A NUMBER
    `itemizes`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `itemized deductions`                 IS A NUMBER
    `taxpayer 65 or over`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `taxpayer blind`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `spouse 65 or over`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `spouse blind`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `dependents`                          IS A NUMBER
    `eligible for the working family credit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earned income`                       IS A NUMBER
    `qualifying children under 18`        IS A NUMBER
    `qualifying older children`           IS A NUMBER
    `factors`                             IS AN `Inflation factors`

-- 290.01, subd. 19(b): net income is federal AGI "with the modifications provided in sections 290.0131, 290.0132, and
-- 290.0135 to 290.0137"; 290.0132, subd. 19: the standard deduction is a subtraction, or by election the itemized
-- deductions "in lieu"; subd. 20: the dependent exemption is a subtraction. Subd. 22(1): for a resident, taxable net income
-- is "the same as net income". Where the person itemizes, the itemized figure is taken as given after 290.0122, subd. 2.
GIVEN `r` IS A `My Minnesota return`
GIVETH A `My Minnesota tax`
`the tax on my Minnesota return` MEANS
    `My Minnesota tax` WITH
        `net income`                                 IS `net`
        `tax before credits`                         IS `tax`
        `child tax credit and working family credit` IS `credits`
        `tax after credits, or refund if negative`   IS `tax` MINUS `credits`
    WHERE
        `status` MEANS `r`'s `filing status`
        `AGI` MEANS `r`'s `federal adjusted gross income`
        `standard` MEANS `the deduction after the high-income limit` `status` `AGI` (`the standard deduction before the limit` `status` (`r`'s `taxpayer 65 or over`) (`r`'s `taxpayer blind`) (`r`'s `spouse 65 or over`) (`r`'s `spouse blind`) (`r`'s `factors`)) (`r`'s `factors`)
        `deduction` MEANS IF `r`'s `itemizes` THEN `r`'s `itemized deductions` ELSE `standard`
        `net` MEANS
            `the larger of` 0
                (sum (LIST
                    `AGI`,
                    `r`'s `additions`,
                    0 MINUS `r`'s `other subtractions`,
                    0 MINUS (`the Social Security subtraction` `status` (`r`'s `taxable Social Security benefits`) `AGI` (`r`'s `provisional income`) (`r`'s `factors`)),
                    0 MINUS `deduction`,
                    0 MINUS (`the dependent exemption` `status` (`r`'s `dependents`) `AGI` (`r`'s `factors`))))
        `tax` MEANS `the tax under 290.06, subd. 2c` `status` `net` (`r`'s `factors`)
        `credits` MEANS `the combined credits after the phaseout` `status` (`r`'s `eligible for the working family credit`) (`r`'s `earned income`) `AGI` (`r`'s `qualifying children under 18`) (`r`'s `qualifying older children`) (`r`'s `factors`)

GIVEN `resident all year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `dependent of another taxpayer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `separate return and spouse itemizes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Why not covered`
`the gap this Minnesota return falls into` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `resident all year`) THEN JUST `a nonresident or part-year resident is not encoded (290.06, subd. 2c(e))`
        IF `dependent of another taxpayer` THEN JUST `an individual who is a dependent of another taxpayer is not encoded (290.0123, subd. 3)`
        IF `separate return and spouse itemizes` THEN JUST `a married individual filing separately whose spouse itemizes has no standard deduction (290.0123, subd. 4(1)); itemized deductions for that case are not encoded`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Questions for the taxpayer`

@export How much Minnesota income tax do I owe for the year as a full-year resident, after the child tax credit and working family credit (a negative answer is a refund)?
GIVEN `resident all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a Minnesota resident for the whole year
      `someone's dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can be claimed as a dependent on another person's federal return
      `separate return, spouse itemizes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are married filing separately and your spouse itemizes deductions
      `filing status` IS A STRING @desc Your federal filing status. One of: "single", "married filing separately", "married filing jointly", "head of household", "surviving spouse"
      `federal AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income for the year, in US dollars
      `additions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your Minnesota additions (290.0131), in US dollars; 0 if none
      `other subtractions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your Minnesota subtractions other than Social Security, the standard or itemized deduction and the dependent exemption (290.0132), in US dollars; 0 if none
      `taxable Social Security` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable part of your Social Security benefits included in federal AGI, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `provisional income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your provisional income: modified AGI under IRC s 86(b)(2) plus half of your taxable Social Security benefits, in US dollars; 0 if no benefits
      `itemizes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you elect to itemize deductions for Minnesota instead of taking the standard deduction
      `itemized deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc If you itemize: your Minnesota itemized deductions after the high-income limit of 290.0122, subd. 2, in US dollars; else 0
      `65 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were 65 or older by the end of the year
      `blind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were blind at the end of the year
      `spouse 65 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse was 65 or older by the end of the year (and qualifies for an exemption under IRC s 151(b))
      `spouse blind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse was blind at the end of the year (and qualifies for an exemption under IRC s 151(b))
      `dependents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependents (IRC ss 151, 152) you claim
      `credit eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would be eligible for the federal earned income credit, ignoring its income limits and s 32(m); a taxpayer with no qualifying children aged 19 to 64 also counts
      `earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your earned income for the year, in US dollars
      `children under 18` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying children (earned income credit rules) under 18 you have
      `older children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying children aged 18 or older in the year you have
      `factor since 2019` IS A NUMBER @desc The section 270C.22 inflation adjustment from 2019 for the year (1 for 2019)
      `factor since 2023` IS A NUMBER @desc The section 270C.22 inflation adjustment from 2023 for the year (1 for 2023)
      `factor since 2025` IS A NUMBER @desc The section 270C.22 inflation adjustment from 2025 for the year (1 for 2025)
GIVETH AN `Answer` `My Minnesota tax`
`How much Minnesota income tax do I owe` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the gap this Minnesota return falls into` `resident all year` `someone's dependent` `separate return, spouse itemizes`
    WHEN JUST `reason` THEN `not covered` `reason`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `answered` (`the tax on my Minnesota return` (`My Minnesota return` WITH
        `filing status`                          IS `the filing status named` `filing status`
        `federal adjusted gross income`          IS `federal AGI`
        `additions`                              IS `additions`
        `other subtractions`                     IS `other subtractions`
        `taxable Social Security benefits`       IS `taxable Social Security`
        `provisional income`                     IS `provisional income`
        `itemizes`                               IS `itemizes`
        `itemized deductions`                    IS `itemized deductions`
        `taxpayer 65 or over`                    IS `65 or over`
        `taxpayer blind`                         IS `blind`
        `spouse 65 or over`                      IS `spouse 65 or over`
        `spouse blind`                           IS `spouse blind`
        `dependents`                             IS `dependents`
        `eligible for the working family credit` IS `credit eligible`
        `earned income`                          IS `earned income`
        `qualifying children under 18`           IS `children under 18`
        `qualifying older children`              IS `older children`
        `factors`                                IS `Inflation factors` WITH `since 2019` IS `factor since 2019`, `since 2023` IS `factor since 2023`, `since 2025` IS `factor since 2025`))

@export How much Minnesota income tax is charged on a taxable net income, before credits (290.06, subd. 2c)?
GIVEN `filing status` IS A STRING @desc Your federal filing status. One of: "single", "married filing separately", "married filing jointly", "head of household", "surviving spouse"
      `taxable net income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Minnesota taxable net income, in US dollars
      `factor since 2019` IS A NUMBER @desc The section 270C.22 inflation adjustment from 2019 for the year (1 for 2019)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What Minnesota tax is charged on my income` MEANS
    `the tax under 290.06, subd. 2c` (`the filing status named` `filing status`) `taxable net income` (`Inflation factors` WITH `since 2019` IS `factor since 2019`, `since 2023` IS 1, `since 2025` IS 1)

@export What is my Minnesota standard deduction, after the high-income limit (290.0123)?
GIVEN `filing status` IS A STRING @desc Your federal filing status. One of: "single", "married filing separately", "married filing jointly", "head of household", "surviving spouse"
      `federal AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `65 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were 65 or older by the end of the year
      `blind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were blind at the end of the year
      `spouse 65 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse was 65 or older by the end of the year
      `spouse blind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse was blind at the end of the year
      `factor since 2023` IS A NUMBER @desc The section 270C.22 inflation adjustment from 2023 for the year (1 for 2023)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my Minnesota standard deduction` MEANS
    `the deduction after the high-income limit` `status` `federal AGI` (`the standard deduction before the limit` `status` `65 or over` `blind` `spouse 65 or over` `spouse blind` `factors`) `factors`
    WHERE
        `status` MEANS `the filing status named` `filing status`
        `factors` MEANS `Inflation factors` WITH `since 2019` IS 1, `since 2023` IS `factor since 2023`, `since 2025` IS 1

@export How much Social Security may I subtract for Minnesota (290.0132, subd. 26)?
GIVEN `filing status` IS A STRING @desc Your federal filing status. One of: "single", "married filing separately", "married filing jointly", "head of household", "surviving spouse"
      `taxable Social Security` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable part of your Social Security benefits included in federal AGI, in US dollars
      `federal AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `provisional income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your provisional income: modified AGI under IRC s 86(b)(2) plus half of your taxable Social Security benefits, in US dollars
      `factor since 2023` IS A NUMBER @desc The section 270C.22 inflation adjustment from 2023 for the year (1 for 2023)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much Social Security may I subtract` MEANS
    `the Social Security subtraction` (`the filing status named` `filing status`) `taxable Social Security` `federal AGI` `provisional income` (`Inflation factors` WITH `since 2019` IS 1, `since 2023` IS `factor since 2023`, `since 2025` IS 1)

§§ `The refund of the credits (290.0661, subd. 6; 290.0671, subd. 4)`

-- "If the amount of credit which the claimant is eligible to receive under this section exceeds the claimant's tax liability
-- under this chapter, the commissioner shall refund the excess to the claimant." No time is stated.
DECLARE `Refund party` IS ONE OF `the commissioner of revenue`
DECLARE `Refund act` IS ONE OF
    `refund the excess to the claimant` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the credits` IS A NUMBER
      `tax liability` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Refund party` `Refund act`
`290.0661, subd. 6 and 290.0671, subd. 4 -- the commissioner must refund the excess of the credits` MEANS
    PARTY `the commissioner of revenue`
    MUST  `refund the excess to the claimant` (EXACTLY (`the larger of` 0 (`the credits` MINUS `tax liability`)))
    HENCE FULFILLED
